<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- OstrichChallenge: NO VEHICLE CRAFTING.

     The way out of the hotel is the 4x4 in the basement, and the stalker has its key. A player
     who can craft a bicycle simply rides away without ever meeting him, so every vehicle recipe
     goes, exactly as the Hospital Challenge does it for the rooftop gyro.

     Recipes only. Vehicle parts in loot and anything a trader might sell still need doing. -->
<configs>

    <!-- Bicycle -->
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleBicycleChassis']"/>
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleBicycleHandlebars']"/>
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleBicyclePlaceable']"/>

    <!-- Minibike -->
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleMinibikeChassis']"/>
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleMinibikeHandlebars']"/>
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleMinibikePlaceable']"/>

    <!-- Motorcycle -->
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleMotorcycleChassis']"/>
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleMotorcycleHandlebars']"/>
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleMotorcyclePlaceable']"/>

    <!-- 4x4 Truck: the hotel's own is placed by the mod, it is never built -->
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleTruck4x4Accessories']"/>
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleTruck4x4Chassis']"/>
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleTruck4x4Placeable']"/>

    <!-- Gyrocopter -->
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleGyroCopterAccessories']"/>
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleGyroCopterChassis']"/>
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='vehicleGyrocopterPlaceable']"/>

    <!-- ============================================================
         NO LAND CLAIM BLOCK
         There is one building and one run: a claim block has no place in it.
         ============================================================ -->
    <remove xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='keystoneBlock']"/>

    <!-- ============================================================
         NO BUCKET ON THE BENCH (v1.30.0)

         Decided 23 September, built 3 October. Fril, mid-test on 2 Oct: "The bucket is still
         craftable. Im not sure if I asked you to remove that." He had not asked, he had DECIDED
         it, and ten days of builds went by with nothing checking the difference between a
         decision written in the devlog and a decision in the files.

         LOOT IS DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED. Only the recipe goes. Fril, 3 Oct: "Leave in loot but
         honestly, Ive never seen one in loot."

         AND THE REASONING ON RECORD WAS WRONG, so it is corrected here rather than repeated.
         The 23 Sep note said the bucket's "only uses are filling itself and building sinks and
         toilets, both pointless in a hotel, so water means the river". Fril, 3 Oct: "there isnt
         a river anywhere close but there are fountains outside the front and there are 2 baths,
         a swimming pool and a jaccuzzi that could be used with a bucket. So it has to go."

         That inverts the point of the change. The bucket is not pointless here, it is the key to
         a swimming pool, a jacuzzi, two baths and the fountains at the front door. Removing the
         CRAFT is what makes those worth something: you cannot bench your way to water, you have
         to find a bucket in the building first. Leaving it in loot is therefore not a softening
         of the decision, it is the whole mechanism.
         ============================================================ -->
    <remove xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='bucketEmpty']"/>

    <!-- ============================================================
         DUKES FROM PRECIOUS METALS
         Silver, gold and diamonds can be turned into money.
         ============================================================ -->
    <append xpath="/recipes">
        <recipe name="casinoCoin" count="100" craft_time="60">
            <ingredient name="resourceSilverNugget" count="1"/>
        </recipe>
        <recipe name="casinoCoin" count="250" craft_time="60">
            <ingredient name="resourceGoldNugget" count="1"/>
        </recipe>
        <recipe name="casinoCoin" count="500" craft_time="60">
            <ingredient name="resourceRawDiamond" count="1"/>
        </recipe>
    </append>

    <!-- ============================================================
         VENDING MACHINE REPAIR KIT

         v1.236.0: NOW GENUINELY CRAFTABLE FROM THE START, IN YOUR INVENTORY.

         Fril, 11 Nov: "Change vending machine recipes to unlock from the start in your
         inventory". He was right and the old comment below was wrong about its own recipe.

         THE CONTRADICTION THAT WAS SITTING HERE. The note said "craftable from the start: a
         security guard putting the staff soda machine back together is a day one job", and
         then the recipe carried craft_area="workbench". A workbench is craftingWorkstations
         level 10, so on day one this was not craftable at all. The intent was written down
         and the attribute quietly disagreed with it.

         WHAT CHANGED: craft_area="workbench" removed, nothing else. A recipe with no
         craft_area is craftable in the backpack, which is 198 of vanilla's 642 recipes, so
         this is the ordinary shape rather than a trick.

         NOT LOCKED BEHIND ANYTHING, verified rather than assumed: this recipe has never had
         an unlocked_by or a learnable flag, so the workbench was the ONLY gate on it. Taking
         the workbench away is the whole of "unlock from the start".

         craft_time stays at 30 seconds. It is NOT tagged packMuleCrafting, deliberately: that
         tag only lets the Pack Mule perk cut crafting time by up to half, the mod's own
         casinoCoin recipes do not carry it, and adding a perk interaction he did not ask for
         would be a silent change. One word to add if he ever wants it.
         ============================================================ -->
    <!-- ============================================================
         INGREDIENTS CHANGED IN v1.237.0, AND THIS IS WHAT FINISHES THE DAY ONE JOB.

         Fril, 11 Nov: "Change the vending machine repair kit recipe to use forged iron, not
         forged steel and replace Springs with Duct tape".

             resourceForgedSteel 6  ->  resourceForgedIron 6
             resourceSpring      5  ->  resourceDuctTape   5

         Counts untouched, he did not ask for that.

         WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN IT LOOKS. Removing craft_area="workbench" above took the
         workbench off the recipe, but the INGREDIENTS were still gated far later than day one,
         so "craftable from the start" was still only half true. Read out of vanilla's recipes:

             resourceForgedSteel   craft_area="forge"  craft_tool="toolForgeCrucible"
                                   The crucible is craftingWorkstations level 75 of 75.
             resourceForgedIron    craft_area="forge", no tool. The forge is level 4.
             resourceSpring        NO RECIPE AT ALL. Salvage only, and nothing else.
             resourceDuctTape      no craft_area, so the backpack. 1 glue + 7 cloth.

         So the old recipe asked for one thing you could not craft before level 75 and one thing
         you could not craft at all. Both are now early or makeable, and the kit is genuinely a
         day one job for the first time, which is what its comment has claimed since v1.13.x.

         WHAT A WRENCHED MACHINE STILL GIVES, re-read from blocks.xml rather than carried over.
         cntVendingMachine2Broken is the parent of all four POI machines and drops:

             resourceElectricParts   2-6      asked for: 10
             resourceMechanicalParts 2-4      asked for: 10
             resourceForgedIron      1-3      asked for: 6     <- NEW pinch point
             resourceForgedSteel     2-3      no longer asked for
             resourceSpring          1-3      no longer asked for
             resourceScrapPolymers   2-5      deliberately not asked for

         SO THE SALVAGE MATHS BARELY MOVES, which is the point: forged iron is 1-3 a machine
         where springs were 1-3, so three machines still covers a kit on decent rolls and four
         on poor ones. The pinch point moves from springs to forged iron and stays about the
         same size. Fril's original numbers survive intact.

         DUCT TAPE IS THE ONE THING MACHINES DO NOT DROP, stated plainly rather than buried.
         It has to be looted or made, and making 5 costs 5 glue and 35 cloth, with the glue
         needing a campfire and a cooking pot (7 bones each, so 35 bones). Cloth is everywhere
         in a hotel. This is a real cost but an early-game one, and unlike springs it is a cost
         the player can CHOOSE to pay rather than wait for a drop.

         Vanilla caps a recipe at five ingredients, hence four and not the full six.
         ============================================================ -->
    <append xpath="/recipes">
        <recipe name="occVendingRepairKit" count="1" craft_time="30">
            <ingredient name="resourceElectricParts" count="10"/>
            <ingredient name="resourceMechanicalParts" count="10"/>
            <ingredient name="resourceForgedIron" count="6"/>
            <ingredient name="resourceDuctTape" count="5"/>
        </recipe>
    </append>

    <!-- ============================================================
         FARM PLOTS, CHEAPER
         No rotting flesh, and 16 each of nitrate and clay.
         ============================================================ -->
    <remove xpath="//recipe[@name='farmPlotBlockVariantHelper']/ingredient[@name='foodRottingFlesh']"/>
    <set xpath="//recipe[@name='farmPlotBlockVariantHelper']/ingredient[@name='resourcePotassiumNitratePowder']/@count">16</set>
    <set xpath="//recipe[@name='farmPlotBlockVariantHelper']/ingredient[@name='resourceClayLump']/@count">16</set>

    <!-- ============================================================
         SEEDS, 2 OF THE CROP EACH
         Farming worth doing without being free.
         ============================================================ -->
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='plantedAloe1']/ingredient/@count">2</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='plantedBlueberry1']/ingredient/@count">2</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='plantedCoffee1']/ingredient/@count">2</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='plantedCorn1']/ingredient/@count">2</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='plantedMushroom1']/ingredient[@name='foodCropMushrooms']/@count">2</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='plantedPotato1']/ingredient/@count">2</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='plantedPumpkin1']/ingredient/@count">2</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='plantedYucca1']/ingredient/@count">2</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='plantedCotton1']/ingredient/@count">2</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='plantedGoldenrod1']/ingredient/@count">2</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='plantedChrysanthemum1']/ingredient/@count">2</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='plantedHop1']/ingredient/@count">2</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='plantedGraceCorn1']/ingredient/@count">2</set>

    <!-- ============================================================
         ARROWS (v1.12.1)

         A wooden arrow, and feathers out of the arrow recipes.

         VERIFIED AGAINST VANILLA recipes.xml AND progression.xml, which Fril supplied after
         v1.12.0 shipped with both of these guessed. Both guesses were wrong in useful ways.

         ONLY TWO ARROWS USE FEATHERS, not the five v1.12.0 patched:
             ammoArrowStone     resourceRockSmall x1, resourceWood x1, resourceFeather x1
             ammoArrowIron      resourceArrowHeadIron x1, resourceWood x1, resourceFeather x1
         SteelAP, Flaming and Exploding already use resourceScrapPolymers, so those three sets
         were inert. Removed rather than left in, because a line that looks like it does
         something and does not is worse than no line.

         AND THE BUNDLES, WHICH v1.12.0 MISSED ENTIRELY. The bulk recipes want EIGHTY feathers
         each, so patching only the singles would have left bulk crafting still demanding them:
             ammoBundleArrowStone   resourceFeather x80
             ammoBundleArrowIron    resourceFeather x80

         v1.13.0: THE BOLTS ARE DONE TOO, on Fril's word, with a wood variant to match. Same
         four shapes as the arrows, and verified against vanilla the same way:
             ammoCrossbowBoltStone / Iron         resourceFeather x1
             ammoBundleCrossbowBoltStone / Iron   resourceFeather x80

         STILL NOT TOUCHED: foodChickenNuggets uses 2 feathers. That is food, not ammunition,
         and feathers remain lootable, so it is left alone deliberately.

         NO PROGRESSION ENTRY IS NEEDED. progression.xml gates only ammoArrowExploding,
         ammoArrowSteelAP and ammoArrowFlaming behind RecipeTagUnlocked. Stone and Iron are
         ungated, and ammoArrowWood is declared with the same shape as Stone, so it is
         craftable from the start.
         ============================================================ -->
    <append xpath="/recipes">
        <recipe name="ammoArrowWood" count="1" craft_time="1.4" tags="packMuleCrafting">
            <ingredient name="resourceWood" count="1"/>
            <ingredient name="resourceScrapPolymers" count="1"/>
        </recipe>

        <!-- v1.13.0: the bolt, same cost as the arrow. Vanilla charges the same for a stone
             bolt as a stone arrow, so matching that keeps the two in step. -->
        <recipe name="ammoCrossbowBoltWood" count="1" craft_time="1.4" tags="packMuleCrafting">
            <ingredient name="resourceWood" count="1"/>
            <ingredient name="resourceScrapPolymers" count="1"/>
        </recipe>
    </append>

    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='ammoArrowStone']/ingredient[@name='resourceFeather']/@name">resourceScrapPolymers</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='ammoArrowIron']/ingredient[@name='resourceFeather']/@name">resourceScrapPolymers</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='ammoBundleArrowStone']/ingredient[@name='resourceFeather']/@name">resourceScrapPolymers</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='ammoBundleArrowIron']/ingredient[@name='resourceFeather']/@name">resourceScrapPolymers</set>

    <!-- v1.13.0: the bolts -->
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='ammoCrossbowBoltStone']/ingredient[@name='resourceFeather']/@name">resourceScrapPolymers</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='ammoCrossbowBoltIron']/ingredient[@name='resourceFeather']/@name">resourceScrapPolymers</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='ammoBundleCrossbowBoltStone']/ingredient[@name='resourceFeather']/@name">resourceScrapPolymers</set>
    <set xpath="/recipes/recipe[@name='ammoBundleCrossbowBoltIron']/ingredient[@name='resourceFeather']/@name">resourceScrapPolymers</set>

</configs>
